1
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:16,175
This is Mempire, live on Monad testnet.

2
00:00:16,366 --> 00:00:17,600
Every coin is a fighter,

3
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,553
and that strip is Monad itself:

4
00:00:19,745 --> 00:00:22,325
blocks voted in about three hundred milliseconds,

5
00:00:22,345 --> 00:00:24,766
and final in under six hundred.

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,391
Sign-up is one passkey prompt,

7
00:00:27,411 --> 00:00:28,297
through Mera.

8
00:00:28,317 --> 00:00:30,680
No seed phrase, no extension.

9
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,206
In about ten seconds,

10
00:00:33,226 --> 00:00:35,354
the relayer mints an eight-card starter deck

11
00:00:35,374 --> 00:00:38,013
on chain, with test AUSD and a

12
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:39,792
little MON for gas.

13
00:00:40,967 --> 00:00:43,037
Minting a new fighter pulls a live

14
00:00:43,057 --> 00:00:45,489
Pyth price into the same transaction.

15
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:49,623
The side boards are the market meta,

16
00:00:49,643 --> 00:00:52,622
written on chain by Chainlink CRE.

17
00:00:53,068 --> 00:00:55,452
We stake the one-dollar tier in MON,

18
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,289
and queue a ranked match.

19
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,765
Every card I drop is its own

20
00:01:00,785 --> 00:01:03,587
Monad transaction, signed by a per-match session

21
00:01:03,607 --> 00:01:05,923
key, so there are no popups.

22
00:01:06,184 --> 00:01:08,501
Each pill shows the real round trip:

23
00:01:08,634 --> 00:01:10,706
executed, then final.

24
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:17,887
We fast-forward.

25
00:01:17,907 --> 00:01:19,458
And a tower falls.

26
00:01:21,967 --> 00:01:23,192
Pot secured!

27
00:01:23,639 --> 00:01:25,639
The second player's claim settles the pot

28
00:01:25,659 --> 00:01:26,548
on chain:

29
00:01:26,623 --> 00:01:27,880
ninety percent to the winner,

30
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:29,462
plus a chest.

31
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,873
Clans and clan wars score only staked

32
00:01:34,893 --> 00:01:36,653
wins verified on chain.

33
00:01:37,007 --> 00:01:38,798
These clans were seeded by our team

34
00:01:38,818 --> 00:01:40,008
for the demo.

35
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,271
Empire holds the leaderboard,

36
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:45,880
reads Monad's staking precompile live,

37
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:48,353
and verifies a passkey signature with Monad's

38
00:01:48,373 --> 00:01:50,527
P-256 precompile.

39
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:54,362
So, what is live on Monad?

40
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:57,535
Chainlink CRE writes the market meta:

41
00:01:57,668 --> 00:02:00,376
thirty-six fighters, signed by the workflow,

42
00:02:00,396 --> 00:02:02,887
accepted only from its forwarder.

43
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,307
Pyth prices every mint,

44
00:02:06,327 --> 00:02:08,969
verified on chain in the same transaction.

45
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:11,999
Gasless chests:

46
00:02:12,019 --> 00:02:15,610
an EIP-7702 authorization, our own paymaster,

47
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:17,227
and the canonical EntryPoint.

48
00:02:17,673 --> 00:02:19,641
The player spends no MON.

49
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:24,886
Passkeys, checked by Monad's P-256 precompile,

50
00:02:24,906 --> 00:02:26,584
at a fraction of the gas.

51
00:02:28,433 --> 00:02:30,085
Every card you play is logged on

52
00:02:30,105 --> 00:02:32,120
chain, from a session key.

53
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:35,561
And every staked match is settled by

54
00:02:35,581 --> 00:02:37,096
the contract itself.

55
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:40,039
Six power-ups.

56
00:02:40,059 --> 00:02:41,691
All live on Monad testnet.

57
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,642
Mempire.

58
00:02:43,662 --> 00:02:44,919
Every coin is a fighter.

59
00:02:44,939 --> 00:02:46,591
Play now, at mempire monad,

60
00:02:46,611 --> 00:02:48,405
dot vercel, dot app.
